impetus.options.simulation_distance.name=Simulation Distance
impetus.options.simulation_distance.disabled_tooltip=This Minecraft version does not have a separate simulation distance; ticking distance follows the loaded world and server rules.
impetus.options.simulation_distance.value=Same as Render Distance
impetus.options.use_quad_normals_for_lighting.name=Use Accurate Quad Shading
impetus.options.use_quad_normals_for_lighting.tooltip=When enabled, Impetus will apply shading to non-vanilla block faces based on the true direction they are facing, not their axis-aligned direction. This can improve lighting quality when the Forge experimental light pipeline is disabled (which is recommended for best performance).\n\nIt has no effect if the experimental light pipeline is enabled.
impetus.options.use_render_pass_optimization.name=Use Block Render Pass Culling
impetus.options.use_render_pass_optimization.tooltip=When enabled, Impetus will detect block model faces that are marked as transparent (or translucent) when the texture is actually opaque (or transparent) and automatically use a more optimal render pass for them.\n\nThis optimization has no effect when a shader pack is active.
impetus.options.use_render_pass_consolidation.name=Use Render Pass Consolidation
impetus.options.use_render_pass_consolidation.tooltip=Combines some vanilla render passes into a single pass. This can very significantly reduce the total number of draw calls needed to render the world, with no visual impact. However, the total amount of rendered geometry will be the same.
impetus.options.inactivity_fps_limit.tooltip=Controls how the game limits framerate when inactive. Minimized only limits the framerate if the game is minimized. AFK also limits the framerate if the player is inactive for long enough.
impetus.options.use_faster_clouds.name=Use Faster Clouds
impetus.options.use_faster_clouds.tooltip=When enabled, Impetus replaces vanilla cloud rendering with a less glitchy and potentially faster implementation. Disable this if mods' cloud customizations aren't visible.
impetus.options.async_graph_search.name=Async Occlusion Culling
impetus.options.async_graph_search.tooltip=Performs occlusion/frustum culling asynchronously, up to one frame behind the current camera position. This can improve frametimes, particularly at higher render distances, but at the cost of chunks popping into view if the camera is turned too aggressively.
impetus.options.chunk_fade_in_duration.name=Chunk Fade Time
impetus.options.chunk_fade_in_duration.value=%s ms
impetus.options.chunk_fade_in_duration.tooltip=Controls how long it takes for newly loaded chunks to fully appear. Longer durations create a smoother transition between unloaded and loaded chunks, reducing visual popping, but may make distant terrain appear to 'fade in' more slowly.
impetus.option_impact.low=Low
impetus.option_impact.medium=Medium
impetus.option_impact.high=High
impetus.option_impact.extreme=Extreme
impetus.option_impact.varies=Varies
impetus.options.pages.general=General
impetus.options.pages.quality=Quality
impetus.options.pages.performance=Performance
impetus.options.pages.advanced=Advanced
impetus.options.view_distance.tooltip=The render distance controls how far away terrain will be rendered. Shorter distances mean that less terrain will be rendered improving frame rates.
impetus.options.simulation_distance.tooltip=The simulation distance controls how far away terrain and entities will be loaded and ticked. Shorter distances can reduce the internal server's load and may improve frame rates.
impetus.options.brightness.tooltip=Controls the brightness (gamma) of the game.
impetus.options.gui_scale.tooltip=Sets the maximum scale factor to be used for the user interface. If 'auto' is used then the largest scale factor will always be used.
impetus.options.fullscreen.tooltip=If enabled the game will display in full-screen (if supported).
impetus.options.v_sync.tooltip=If enabled the game's frame rate will be synchronized to the monitor's refresh rate making for a generally smoother experience at the expense of overall input latency. This setting might reduce performance if your system is too slow.
impetus.options.fps_limit.tooltip=Limits the maximum number of frames per second. This can help reduce battery usage and general system load when multi-tasking. If VSync is enabled this option will be ignored unless it is lower than your display's refresh rate.
impetus.options.view_bobbing.tooltip=If enabled the player's view will sway and bob when moving around. Players who experience motion sickness while playing can benefit from disabling this.
impetus.options.attack_indicator.tooltip=Controls where the Attack Indicator is displayed on screen.
impetus.options.autosave_indicator.tooltip=If enabled an indicator will be shown when the game is saving the world to disk.
impetus.options.autosave_indicator.name=Autosave Indicator
impetus.options.autosave_indicator.disabled_tooltip=The modern autosave indicator is not available on this Minecraft version.
impetus.options.graphics_api.name=Graphics API
impetus.options.graphics_api.tooltip=This Minecraft 1.12.2 target uses the OpenGL backend. Vulkan is only represented as an unavailable modern backend here.
impetus.options.graphics_quality.tooltip=The default graphics quality controls some legacy options and is necessary for mod compatibility. If the options below are left to Default they will use this setting.
impetus.options.clouds_quality.tooltip=Controls the presence of rendered clouds in the sky.
impetus.options.cloud_height.name=Cloud Height
impetus.options.cloud_height.value=%s blocks
impetus.options.cloud_height.tooltip=Controls the Y level where vanilla clouds are rendered.
impetus.options.cloud_distance.name=Cloud Distance
impetus.options.cloud_distance.value=%s Chunks
impetus.options.cloud_distance.tooltip=Controls how far away vanilla clouds are rendered.
impetus.options.weather_quality.tooltip=Controls the quality of rain and snow effects.
impetus.options.weather_effect_radius.name=Weather Effect Radius
impetus.options.weather_effect_radius.tooltip=Controls the radius around the camera used for rain and snow effects.
impetus.options.leaves_quality.name=Leaves
impetus.options.leaves_quality.tooltip=Controls the quality of leaves.
impetus.options.see_through_leaves.name=See-Through Leaves
impetus.options.see_through_leaves.tooltip=Controls whether leaves use the fancy, see-through rendering mode.
impetus.options.particle_quality.tooltip=Controls the maximum number of particles which can be present on screen at any one time.
impetus.options.smooth_lighting.tooltip=Controls whether blocks will be smoothly lit and shaded. This slightly increases the amount of time needed to re-build a chunk but doesn't affect frame rates.
impetus.options.biome_blend.value=%s block(s)
impetus.options.biome_blend.tooltip=Controls the range which biomes will be sampled for block colorization. Higher values greatly increase the amount of time it takes to build chunks for diminishing improvements in quality.\nNot compatible with the Better/Betterer Biome Blend mod
impetus.options.entity_distance.name=Entity Distance
impetus.options.entity_distance.tooltip=Controls how far away entities can render from the player. Higher values increase the render distance at the expense of frame rates.
impetus.options.entity_shadows.tooltip=If enabled basic shadows will be rendered beneath mobs and other entities.
impetus.options.vignette.name=Show Vignette
impetus.options.vignette.tooltip=If enabled a vignette effect will be rendered on the player's view. This is very unlikely to make a difference to frame rates unless you are fill-rate limited.
impetus.options.mipmap_levels.tooltip=Controls the number of mipmaps which will be used for block model textures. Higher values provide better rendering of blocks in the distance but may adversely affect performance with many animated textures.
impetus.options.texel_interpolation.name=Texel Interpolation
impetus.options.texel_interpolation.value=Nearest
impetus.options.texel_interpolation.tooltip=Texel interpolation is fixed to nearest-neighbor sampling for vanilla pixel-art textures.
impetus.options.improved_transparency.name=Improved Transparency
impetus.options.improved_transparency.tooltip=Modern improved-transparency controls are not available on this target; use the translucent face sorting option below for 1.12.2 transparency ordering.
impetus.options.use_block_face_culling.name=Use Block Face Culling
impetus.options.use_block_face_culling.tooltip=If enabled only the sides of blocks which are facing the camera will be submitted for rendering. This can eliminate a large number of block faces very early in the rendering process saving memory bandwidth and time on the GPU. Some resource packs may have issues with this option so try disabling it if you're seeing holes in blocks.
impetus.options.use_compact_vertex_format.name=Use Compact Vertex Format
impetus.options.use_compact_vertex_format.tooltip=If enabled a more compact vertex format will be used for rendering chunks. This can reduce graphics memory usage and bandwidth requirements significantly especially for integrated graphics cards but can cause z-fighting with some resource packs due to how it reduces the precision of position and texture coordinate attributes.
impetus.options.translucent_face_sorting.name=Translucent Face Sorting
impetus.options.translucent_face_sorting.tooltip=If enabled translucent effects from surfaces such as stained glass and water will be applied correctly.
impetus.options.block_transparency.name=Block Transparency...
impetus.options.fluid_culling.name=Fluid Culling
impetus.options.fluid_culling.value=Optimized
impetus.options.fluid_culling.tooltip=Controls how hidden fluid faces are skipped during chunk building. The 1.12.2 renderer uses the optimized mode.
impetus.options.fluid_shaping.name=Fluid Shaping
impetus.options.fluid_shaping.value=Vanilla
impetus.options.fluid_shaping.tooltip=Controls how fluid edges are shaped. The 1.12.2 renderer keeps vanilla fluid shaping for compatibility.
impetus.options.entity_sorting.name=Entity Sorting
impetus.options.entity_sorting.value=Enhanced
impetus.options.entity_sorting.tooltip=Controls how entities are ordered for rendering. The 1.12.2 renderer uses the enhanced visibility-aware path.
impetus.options.fast_block_renderer.name=Use Fast Block Renderer
impetus.options.fast_block_renderer.tooltip=Enables the backported faster block renderer from modern Impetus versions, which has better performance but may look slightly different.
impetus.options.use_fog_occlusion.name=Use Fog Occlusion
impetus.options.use_fog_occlusion.tooltip=If enabled chunks which are determined to be fully hidden by fog effects will not be rendered helping to improve performance. The improvement can be more dramatic when fog effects are heavier (such as while underwater) but it may cause undesirable visual artifacts between the sky and fog in some scenarios.
impetus.options.use_entity_culling.name=Use Entity Culling
impetus.options.use_entity_culling.tooltip=If enabled entities determined not to be in any visible chunks will be skipped during rendering. This can help improve performance by avoiding the rendering of entities located underground or behind walls.
impetus.options.animate_only_visible_textures.name=Animate Only Visible Textures
impetus.options.animate_only_visible_textures.tooltip=If enabled only animated textures determined to be visible will be updated. This can provide a significant boost to frame rates on some hardware especially with heavier resource packs. If you experience issues with some textures not being animated try disabling this option.
impetus.options.cpu_render_ahead_limit.name=CPU Render-Ahead Limit
impetus.options.cpu_render_ahead_limit.tooltip=Specifies the maximum number of frames the CPU can be waiting on the GPU to finish rendering. Very low or high values may create frame rate instability.
impetus.options.cpu_render_ahead_limit.value=%s frame(s)
impetus.options.memory_tracing.name=Memory Tracing
impetus.options.memory_tracing.tooltip=Records allocation stack traces for native buffers. This is useful for debugging leaks but may add overhead.
impetus.options.inactivity_fps_limit.name=Reduce FPS When
impetus.options.inactivity_fps_limit.value=AFK
impetus.options.inactivity_fps_limit.disabled_tooltip=Automatic inactivity FPS limiting is not implemented on this 1.12.2 target.
impetus.options.show_toasts.name=Show In-Game Notifications
impetus.options.show_toasts.tooltip=Shows Impetus compatibility warnings as small in-game notifications instead of only writing them to the log.
impetus.options.incompatible_pack_warnings.name=Resource Pack Warnings
impetus.options.incompatible_pack_warnings.tooltip=Warns when an active resource pack contains shader program assets that may conflict with Impetus or Iris-style rendering.
impetus.options.performance_impact_string=Performance Impact: %s
impetus.options.use_persistent_mapping.name=Use Persistent Mapping
impetus.options.use_persistent_mapping.tooltip=If enabled a small amount of memory will be persistently mapped as a staging buffer for chunk uploading helping to reduce CPU overhead and frame time instability when loading or updating chunks.\n\nRequires OpenGL 4.4 or ARB_buffer_storage.
impetus.options.chunk_update_threads.name=Chunk Update Threads
impetus.options.chunk_update_threads.tooltip=Specifies the number of threads to use for chunk building. Using more threads can speed up chunk loading and update speed but may negatively impact frame times.
impetus.options.chunk_updates.name=Chunk Updates
impetus.options.always_defer_chunk_updates.name=Always Defer Chunk Updates
impetus.options.always_defer_chunk_updates.tooltip=If enabled rendering will never wait for chunk updates to finish even if they are important. This can greatly improve frame rates in some scenarios but it may create significant visual lag in the world.
impetus.options.use_no_error_context.name=Use No Error Context
impetus.options.use_no_error_context.tooltip=If enabled the OpenGL context will be created with error checking disabled. This may slightly improve performance but it also increases the risk that the game will crash instead of gracefully handling OpenGL errors. You should disable this option if you are experiencing sudden unexplained crashes.
impetus.options.use_no_error_context.disabled_tooltip=No-error OpenGL contexts are not exposed by this 1.12.2 LWJGL2 backend.
