impetus.options.quad_splitting.name=Quad Splitting
impetus.options.quad_splitting.tooltip=Uses exact BSP ordering for translucent geometry within a chunk, eliminating most translucency sorting artifacts at a small meshing cost. When disabled, a faster centroid distance sort is used.
impetus.options.quad_splitting.disabled=Disabled
impetus.options.quad_splitting.enabled=Enabled

impetus.options.pages.memory=Memory
impetus.options.coartatio.resource_locations.name=Deduplicate Resource Names
impetus.options.coartatio.resource_locations.tooltip=Shares the namespace and path strings behind every ResourceLocation. A modded instance holds hundreds of thousands of these, and the namespace is one of a few hundred mod IDs repeated over and over.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.model_variants.name=Deduplicate Model Variants
impetus.options.coartatio.model_variants.tooltip=Shares the variant string of every ModelResourceLocation. "normal" and "inventory" alone account for most of them.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.quad_vertex_data.name=Pool Quad Vertex Data
impetus.options.coartatio.quad_vertex_data.tooltip=Every block face bakes to a 28-integer vertex array, and identical geometry produces byte-identical arrays. Pooling them collapses millions down to tens of thousands.\n\nQuads whose vertex data may be rewritten later are never pooled, so this cannot corrupt rendering.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.multipart_conditions.name=Flatten Multipart Conditions
impetus.options.coartatio.multipart_conditions.tooltip=Multipart blockstates (fences, walls, panes, wires, pipes) compile to a tree of predicate objects, one set per block. This flattens each tree into a single object holding arrays, then shares identical ones between blocks.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.block_states.name=Compress Block States
impetus.options.coartatio.block_states.tooltip=The single largest saving available. Vanilla gives every block state its own lookup table mapping each property value to the resulting state — hundreds of megabytes of pure redundancy in a large pack.\n\nThis replaces the table with one packed integer per state and one shared array per block. Any block the packer cannot handle silently keeps vanilla states.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.state_properties.name=Compact State Property Maps
impetus.options.coartatio.state_properties.tooltip=Shares one property-key array across every state of a block, so each state stores only its values.\n\nRequires Compress Block States, and a JVM that permits the necessary class injection. Falls back to the standard map if either is unavailable.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.nbt_backing_map.name=Compact NBT Storage
impetus.options.coartatio.nbt_backing_map.tooltip=NBT is the most numerous object graph in a modded save: every item stack, tile entity, entity and packet. Vanilla gives each compound a full hash map even though most hold four or five entries.\n\nThis uses flat array storage for small compounds and promotes to a hash map only when one grows.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.nbt_keys.name=Share NBT Keys
impetus.options.coartatio.nbt_keys.tooltip=NBT keys are drawn from a tiny shared vocabulary — id, Count, Damage, tag, x, y, z — but every compound normally holds its own copy of each string. This shares them.\n\nApplies to compounds created from now on.
impetus.options.coartatio.nbt_threshold.name=NBT Array Storage Limit
impetus.options.coartatio.nbt_threshold.tooltip=Entry count at which an NBT compound switches from flat array storage to a hash map. Array storage is smaller and faster to search at small sizes; a hash map wins once a compound grows past this.\n\nSet to 0 to always use hash maps.\n\nApplies to compounds created from now on.
impetus.options.coartatio.baked_models.name=Compact Baked Models
impetus.options.coartatio.baked_models.tooltip=Replaces the growable lists and maps inside baked models with exactly-sized immutable ones, removing the unused growth capacity every model carries.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.model_graph.name=Compact Model Registry
impetus.options.coartatio.model_graph.tooltip=Swaps the model loader's hash maps for a more compact implementation. The largest holds one entry per blockstate variant — tens of thousands in a large pack.\n\nMaps whose ordering affects which model wins a collision are left alone.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.chunk_nbt.name=Strip Loaded Chunk Data
impetus.options.coartatio.chunk_nbt.tooltip=Chunks are loaded in two stages, and the entire chunk tag — tens of kilobytes of block and light arrays — stays in memory between them even though it has already been copied out.\n\nThis drops everything the second stage does not read.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.empty_sections.name=Drop Empty Chunk Sections
impetus.options.coartatio.empty_sections.tooltip=A chunk section whose blocks have all been mined out still loads a full block-state container and light arrays, roughly ten kilobytes for pure air.\n\nSections are only dropped when their lighting can be recomputed exactly, so this cannot darken caves or overhangs.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.debug_overlay.name=Show Memory Statistics
impetus.options.coartatio.debug_overlay.tooltip=Adds a Coartatio line to the F3 debug overlay showing how much has been pooled.
impetus.options.coartatio.log_statistics.name=Log Memory Statistics
impetus.options.coartatio.log_statistics.tooltip=Writes a breakdown of every pool to the log after each resource reload. Useful for checking what is actually being shared.
impetus.options.coartatio.class_loader_cache.name=Reclaim Class Loader Cache
impetus.options.coartatio.class_loader_cache.tooltip=The mod loader keeps the raw bytecode of every class it has ever loaded for the entire session, which in a large pack is hundreds of megabytes doing nothing after startup.\n\nThis lets the garbage collector reclaim it while still serving anything that asks later.\n\nUsually the single largest saving available.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.sprite_data.name=Release Texture Pixel Data
impetus.options.coartatio.sprite_data.tooltip=Every stitched texture keeps a full copy of its pixels in memory after the atlas has been uploaded to the graphics card. This releases them.\n\nAnimated textures are left alone, since they need their frames every tick.\n\nDisable this if a texture mod misbehaves.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.model_transforms.name=Share Model Transforms
impetus.options.coartatio.model_transforms.tooltip=Every baked model carries a set of camera transforms and an item override list, and the overwhelming majority of them are identical. This shares one copy between all of them.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.bake_state.name=Release Model Build Data
impetus.options.coartatio.bake_state.tooltip=Frees the unbaked models and load errors the model loader keeps after baking is finished. Released only once every mod has had its chance to read them.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.runtime_collections.name=Compact Runtime Collections
impetus.options.coartatio.runtime_collections.tooltip=Replaces the hash maps behind game registries, entity synced data and the per-chunk entity lookup with more compact implementations.\n\nThe entity ones scale with how much is loaded rather than with any setting.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.search_trees.name=Lazy Creative Search Index
impetus.options.coartatio.search_trees.tooltip=The creative search box builds a full text index over every item in the game at startup and on every resource reload, whether or not you ever search.\n\nThis defers it until the first search. With a recipe-viewer mod installed it is never built at all, since those replace the search UI entirely.\n\nTakes effect after a restart.
impetus.options.coartatio.clear_on_leave.name=Free Pools On Leaving World
impetus.options.coartatio.clear_on_leave.tooltip=Two pools grow while you play rather than while loading: NBT keys, and resource paths from things like downloaded skins. Neither shrinks on its own.\n\nThis frees them when you return to the main menu, so a long session does not carry its strings into the next world.\n\nApplies immediately.
